    "9:1–5 — I say the truth in Christ, I lie not, my conscience also bearing me witness in the Holy Ghost, that I have great heaviness and continual sorrow in my heart. For I could wish that myself were accursed from Christ for my brethren, my kinsmen according to the flesh: who are Israelites; to whom pertaineth the adoption, and the glory, and the covenants, and the giving of the law, and the service of God, and the promises; whose are the fathers, and of whom as concerning the flesh Christ came, who is over all, God blessed for ever. Amen. The man who wrote 8:39 still has a wound. Seven gifts named as Israel’s. Christ according to the flesh is theirs. This chapter does not start with a system. It starts with a curse Paul would take if it would help his people.",
