    "10:1–4 — Brethren, my heart’s desire and prayer to God for Israel is, that they might be saved. For I bear them record that they have a zeal of God, but not according to knowledge. For they being ignorant of God’s righteousness, and going about to establish their own righteousness, have not submitted themselves unto the righteousness of God. For Christ is the end of the law for righteousness to every one that believeth. Desire and prayer — 9’s grief is still on its knees. Zeal granted. Knowledge denied. Own righteousness as a project. Christ is the end — telos: goal and terminus — of the law for righteousness to every believer.",
